+        "capture_speedup_pct": 4.5
+      },
+      "slice2": {
+        "seconds_saved": 87.0,
+        "capture_speedup_pct": 5.7
+      }
+    },
+    "ceilings_on_the_t7_capture": {
+      "if_the_whole_disc_transfer_overlapped_with_the_sd_write_seconds": 1166.0,
+      "speedup_pct_upper_bound": 37.6,
+      "with_slice2_as_well_seconds": 1079.0
+    },
+    "conclusions": [
+      "KOS's CRC16 costs 22.7 cycles a byte of CPU here (worker time; the wall-time cyc_b figures of 24/12/9/25 include the UI's 2 Hz share). The table version costs 11.7, slice2 8.8, nibble 24.9 (slower than KOS's, as predicted from instruction counts). All four return identical values.",
+      "Applied to the T7 capture (write phase 63.8% of the time), slice2 would save about 87 s of 1605: a 5.7% faster capture. This is a projection from the microbenchmark, and the gain is on the capture, not the 8% it would be on the SD write alone.",
